; RockCluster4 — one of 4 Rock terrain cluster variants (D-42 model_scenes variety pass).
; Uses RocksCluster.glb ("Rocks" by Quaternius, CC0, poly.pizza — see
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_poly_pizza_nature.tres), which is ALREADY a
; pre-modeled group of 3 small rocks in one mesh — the source-file equivalent of what the
; other 3 variants build by hand. Plus 1x the small Rock_2.glb offset to the side as a 4th,
; separate piece, so this variant doesn't read as identical in silhouette to a bare
; instance of the source file.
;
; RocksCluster raw measured AABB: footprint 0.304x0.262, height 0.080 tile-units — already
; low and small, so scaled UP (1.8x) for visual presence on a 0.94-unit tile rather than
; scaled down like the other 3 variants; resulting footprint ~0.55x0.47, height ~0.14 —
; still far below the old single giant rock's 0.877 height. FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF: the
; scale-up factor and the extra piece's placement are first-pass judgment calls.
;
; Slab matches the existing Rock terrain grey (Color(0.55, 0.55, 0.58, 1)).
;
; SLAB WIDENED 0.94 -> 1.0 (2026-08-16, human-reported cross-tile seam gap) — same fix,
; same reasoning as CommonTree1.tscn's header. X/Z only, Y (0.2) untouched.
